From 96a82a0b22197fdc20732b6b3ff79116adcd5ce1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 14:25:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02354/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE D
 (CONTINUOUS SELF-LEARNING; mandated; NEW mechanism) -- a game-AGNOSTIC
 ACTION-ROLE / object-interaction encoder for cross-game value transfer
 (ReactiveGWM, arXiv:2605.15256 VERIFIED). .400 (exp4331) found a LEARNED
 FRAME ENCODER yielded NO cross-game transfer (cross_game_state_reduction
 1.008, CI95 [1.0,1.03], positive control passed) -- the 2nd
 cross-game-transfer null (after exp4318's generic features). DIAGNOSIS
 (ReactiveGWM): raw-frame features carry no game-invariant search-value
 signal; the fix is to DECOUPLE action-role / object-interaction structure
 from per-game pixels (a game-agnostic interaction representation that
 transfers zero-shot). Train the action-role encoder over the 11+ solved
 games' traces; re-test LEAVE-ONE-GAME-OUT cross-game value transfer for
 SEARCH EFFICIENCY (does a value head trained on the action-role features of
 the other games reduce search states on the held-out game?). HARD: report
 cross_game_state_reduction under leave-one-game-out + a positive control
 (baseline solves held-out). Emit learned_encoder_transfer_helps BARE bool :=
 (state reduction > 1.0 AND CI95 lower bound > 1.0). verifier_is_oracle=false
 (the learned value head is oracle-distinct). retire_if_same_verdict: true --
 a 3rd null across feature representations (generic, raw-frame, action-role)
 RETIRES the cross-game-transfer-for-search-efficiency direction. NO TRM
 training.

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
